  seed family       offset 104729 -> first creature 000000000136c0e2  (family 0 is the
                    exploratory run; a confirmation MUST show a nonzero offset)
  question          `axiscollide` showed distance does not predict the wipe,
                    but its "orthogonal" arms set the second target's F1 to
                    A's OWN F1 target on the joint metric -- so they REAFFIRM
                    A's axis rather than saying nothing about it. This uses
                    `second_axis` so the gap rewards ONE formant.
  the prediction    `f2-axis` well ABOVE `f1-axis` but BELOW `keep`: A's axis
                    is unconstrained, not maintained. Written before the run.
  what refutes it   `f2-axis` collapsing toward `f1-axis` -- then ANY second
                    lesson wipes A whatever it asks, and the axis account is a
                    description of one special case rather than a mechanism.

